course: dictionary
lesson: 3119
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «The electric kettle boiled in two minutes.» Here electric means working by electricity, because a kettle needs power to boil water.
explain: «The electric current flowed through the wire and lit the bulb.» Electric here means made by electricity. The current is the electricity itself, moving along the wire.
explain: «The atmosphere was electric» is different again. It is not about plugs or wires. It describes a room where everyone feels a thrilling, exciting energy, as if the air itself were buzzing.
explain: To check, swap in your meaning. If "working by electricity" makes sense in the sentence, you have found it. If not, try the next meaning until the sentence makes sense.
fact: «Electric» can describe things that use electricity, such as an electric car.
fact: «Electric» can also describe things made by electricity, such as an electric shock or an electric current.
fact: «Electric» can describe a very exciting feeling, as in «The atmosphere was electric».
fact: Electricity can be dangerous: keep electric things away from the bath and sink, and never fly a kite near power lines.
fact: An electric circuit needs a power source, wires and a complete loop before a bulb will light.
exercise: «The electric kettle boiled in two minutes.» What does electric mean here? | A very exciting feeling | Made of glass | Quiet and slow | *Using or working by electricity
exercise: «The atmosphere was electric before the final goal.» What does electric mean here? | Very quiet and calm | Full of water | *A very exciting feeling | Very cold
exercise: In «an electric shock», what does electric mean? | *Made by electricity | Very old | Quick and light | Written down
test: «An electric car is very quiet.» What does electric mean here? | Shiny and new | Very exciting | Made by a storm | *Using or working by electricity
test: Which sentence uses electric to mean a very exciting feeling? | «The electric fence kept the sheep in.» | *«The atmosphere was electric before the final goal.» | «The electric shock made her jump.»
exam: Which clue in «The electric kettle boiled in two minutes» shows that electric means working by electricity? | *The kettle, a thing that needs power to boil water | The word boiled, which means bubbled | There is no clue at all | The word minutes
